<Docs edit="site/src/pages/help/index.astro" title="FAQ" description="Answers to the questions people ask first about Facet." group="Help" current={url('/help/')} headings={headings}>
  <h2 id="hardware">Panels</h2>
  <h3 id="which-panels">Which panels does Facet run on?</h3>
  <p>
    Two 4 inch square touch panels so far: the Waveshare ESP32-P4-86 and the Guition ESP32-S3-4848S040.
    <a href={url('/panels/')}>Panels</a> compares them, with the numbers measured on each.
  </p>
  <h3 id="other-panels">Will other panels work?</h3>
  <p>
    Not in 1.0. Facet is built and tested on these two so far; other panels come after the release. If you would like to see a panel
    supported, say so on GitHub (<a href={url('/contributing/')}>Contributing</a>).
  </p>

  <h2 id="faq">Questions</h2>
  <h3 id="need-ha">Do I need Home Assistant?</h3>
  <p>
    Yes. Facet is made for Home Assistant: your lights, media players and sensors come from it, and firmware updates
    are offered there.
  </p>
  <h3 id="cloud">Does it need the internet or a cloud account?</h3>
  <p>
    No account. The panel talks to Home Assistant on your own network. Only checking for updates needs the
    internet.
  </p>
  <h3 id="esphome">Do I need to know ESPHome?</h3>
  <p>
    No. You install Facet from the browser on the <a href={url('/install/')}>Install</a> page and set it up from the panel
    and Home Assistant. There is no YAML to write.
  </p>
  <h3 id="own-screens">Can I make my own screens?</h3>
  <p>
    Yes. A screen is a short spec made of Facet's <a href={url('/inside/components/')}>components</a>, so an AI
    assistant can make one for you: <a href={url('/ai/')}>Make screens with AI</a>.
  </p>
  <h3 id="missing">Why is a screen I saw mentioned not on my panel?</h3>
  <p>
    A release only carries the screens that are ready. <a href={url('/updates/#next')}>What's next</a> on the Updates page
    lists what is being built now.
  </p>
  <h3 id="cost">What does it cost?</h3>
  <p>
    Nothing. Facet is open source under the MIT licence (its fonts keep their SIL Open Font Licence). You only need the
    panel. If you enjoy it, you can support it on <a href="https://buymeacoffee.com/mrdarrengriffin">Buy Me a Coffee</a>
    or <a href="https://ko-fi.com/mrdarrengriffin">Ko-fi</a>.
  </p>
</Docs>
